<article class="env-definition" id="0B22">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B22">Definition <span data-tag="0B22">5.30.7</span>.</a> A <em>topological ring</em> is a ring $R$ endowed with a topology such that addition $R \times R \to R$, $(x, y) \mapsto x + y$ and multiplication $R \times R \to R$, $(x, y) \mapsto xy$ are continuous. A <em>homomorphism of topological rings</em> is a homomorphism of rings which is continuous. </p>
</article>